findings.problem:
At the bench the screen shows a lot of text at once:
- the job card (9 words);
- the station panel: a header, a 15–20-word ask sentence and 8–10 key/value rows (~55 words), plus a 'Decoder: S/N ≥ 6 dB… Game tuning values.' footnote;
- a toast of up to 30 words that lasts at least 4 s (e.g. 'Switch-on: the coil's current can't jump. It ramps up (ringing as the capacitor charges), then carries steady DC to the latch.');
- the scope's own sentence repeating the same thing ('Coil current ramps up (it can't jump), then carries steady DC.');
- the prompt.
Values repeat across these: S/N is on the scope and the panel; each can's corner frequency is on its tag, in the panel's Series/Shunt rows, and as a scope line label; the latch state is on the latch lamp and in the panel row. The job asks are method recipes ('Move the cart, reroute the cable, filter the line.', 'Fit and orient the right whip.'). This makes the bench read as a form, and the scope (the best feedback in the room) competes with the panel. Breaks DR-40 (≤25 words), DR-41 (each value once) and DR-39 (goals say what, not how).

The can tags carry the key teaching link between part value and corner frequency. The second line ('↓ 11 kHz', '↓ 3.4 kHz') renders at about 4–5 px cap height at 1440×900, the value line at about 8 px. The tag lies at -1.2 rad on the board, so it is foreshortened. The shunt can's tag is placed over the yellow 'SHUNT' slot sign, which then disappears (only a sliver shows). On the scope:
- the legend ('message noise filter'), the axis labels ('1 kHz', '10 kHz') and the corner labels are 7–9 px;
- two corner labels collide when the corners are close ('2.4 kHz' over '2.3 kHz' with a series C and a shunt C);
- the spectrum, which shows what the filter does, occupies only the bottom third, with bars 6–12 px wide.
Other overlaps:
- the rerouted 'clear' cable spline runs across the RECEIVER plate and jack (the R3A N9 complaint moved from ANTENNA to RECEIVER);
- in the 'past motor' position, the route lever's red knob sits over the '1.5 m' rack caption, which reads '1.5 r'.
Breaks DR-48 (text ≥ 14 px cap) and DR-70/DR-72 (no overlaps).
